# The Node version a contributor should develop against.
#
# Not the floor, and not the newest. `engines` says `>=20.19.0`, and CI runs
# 20.19.0, 22.x, 24.x and 20.x -- but 20.19.0 is the version CI uses to *prove the
# floor still works*, which makes it a poor choice for day-to-day development:
# nobody should be missing a standard library method that Node 22 has while
# writing a feature.
#
# 22.x is the line this repository develops on, and the line the Windows and
# coverage CI legs use. It is the active LTS, it is what most MCP hosts ship, and
# it is the version the two release workflows run `npm run verify:package` on.
# `.nvmrc` exists so that `nvm use` and every editor that reads it agree, because
# the previous answer was "whichever Node you happened to have", and the first
# symptom of that is a contributor reporting a bug that only reproduces on 24.
22.14.0
